course: dictionary
lesson: 4715
title: Hoop: one word, many rings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hoop is a large ring. Hoop can mean different things, so the words around it tell you which one. «Mini-basketball for younger children uses a lower hoop of about 2.60 m» shows that a hoop here is the ring you throw the ball through.
explain: Look for clues. «A hula hoop» and «spin» tell you it is a plastic ring you twirl around your waist. «Players hit wooden balls through small hoops pushed into the grass» tells you the hoops are metal arches in a lawn game. Check your meaning by swapping in the word ring: if the sentence still makes sense, you are right.
explain: Hoop also has a phrase: «jump through hoops». Nobody really jumps through a ring here. It means to do many hard or boring tasks to get something. When a word does not fit its normal meaning, look at the words around it to find the real meaning.
fact: A hoop is a large ring made of wood, metal or plastic.
fact: In basketball, the hoop is the ring and net that you throw the ball through.
fact: «A full-size hoop is 3.05 m (10 feet) high.»
fact: Informally, «hoops» means the game of basketball, as in «shoot hoops».
fact: «Croquet is a lawn game ... through small hoops pushed into the grass; it became hugely popular in England in the 1860s.»
exercise: «A full-size hoop is 3.05 m (10 feet) high.» What is a hoop in this sentence? | A long stick for hitting a ball | *A ring and net that you throw the ball through | A pair of socks
exercise: Ben's mum says, «You must jump through hoops before you can go out.» What does she mean? | He must sing a song | He must jump through a real ring on the floor | He must go out at once | *He must do many hard or boring tasks first
exercise: Maya spins a plastic ring around her waist all afternoon. Which word names it? | Mallet | *Hula hoop | Lawn | Basketball
test: «Players hit wooden balls through small hoops pushed into the grass.» What are the hoops in this sentence? | Long wooden sticks used to hit the balls | Wooden balls that players throw | Pieces of wood for a fire | *Small arches pushed into the grass that balls are hit through
test: Kai says, «I want to shoot hoops after school.» What does hoops mean here? | A plastic ring spun around the waist | A type of circus act | Metal arches on a lawn | *Basketball
exam: Which phrase means to do many hard or boring tasks to get something? | Hula hoop | Shoot hoops | Basketball hoop | *Jump through hoops
